On Sat, Mar 06, 2004 at 09:39:51AM -0800, Brian Parkhurst wrote:
> I've been reading the Gentoo documentation, but recently read a thread that
> stated you can force a build of a masked package.
> How is this accomplished?

Depends on how the package is masked. If emerge says it's masked by
~keyword, then you can force a build by doing
ACCEPT_KEYWORDS="~alpha" emerge <package>

If it's masked by some other methid, you'll have to edit the KEYWORDS line
in the ebuild file. That file is in /usr/portage/<group>/<package-name> ,
under the name <package-name>-<version>.ebuild.

